      "file": "gnutls/lib/nettle/pk.c",
      "function": "get_supported_gost_curve",
      "line": null,
      "code": "case GNUTLS_ECC_CURVE_GOST256CPA:\n\treturn nettle_get_gost_256cpa();\ncase GNUTLS_ECC_CURVE_GOST256CPXA:\n\treturn nettle_get_gost_256cpa();\ncase GNUTLS_ECC_CURVE_GOST256B:\n\treturn nettle_get_gost_256cpa();",
      "note": "The staged patch adds a `NEED_GOSTDSA` capability check, renames the local curve accessors and objects to GC256B/GC512A names, and rewrites `get_supported_gost_curve()` so `GOST256CPA`, `GOST256CPXA`, and `GOST256B` all resolve via the `GOST256B` fallthrough to `nettle_get_gost_gc256b()`, while `GOST512A` resolves to `nettle_get_gost_gc512a()`. It also moves the local-only VKO and unmask declarations into `gostdsa2.h`, so this path no longer returns the old local `_gnutls_gost_256cpa` or `_gnutls_gost_512a` objects.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
